# Opus via background Shell (Cursor main agent)

When this Cursor chat is the **main agent** and needs **Claude Opus**, do
**not** use Cursor `Task` / `claude-opus-*`. Use the local Claude Code wrapper
in a **background Shell**. Policy SoT:
`~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/SKILL.md`
(§ "Opus transport" + § "Cursor-only — Opus / background-worker monitoring").

Session shape with Chase (discuss → mega-issue → this Opus handoff → Grok
land): `~/.cursor/rules/sume-chase-work-loop.mdc`.

## Binary

- Unified wrapper: `agent-human-stream` (Claude Code + Grok Build).
  `claude-human-stream` is a `--backend claude` alias.
  Grok Build CLI: `agent-human-stream --backend grok --name X "prompt"`
- PATH: `claude-human-stream` / `agent-human-stream` →
  `~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/bin/*.sh`
- There is **no** `--cwd` flag. `cd` in the shell command first.
- Wrapper flags go **before** the prompt; extra `claude` / `grok` flags go **after**:
  `claude-human-stream --name X --resume UUID "prompt" --model opus`

## Correct launch pattern (copy this)

**Do not** `Write` a prompt file and `$(cat …)` it from a **parallel** Shell
in the same turn. Cloud Write is not visible to that Shell yet →
`cat: No such file` → wrapper `error: missing prompt` → **exit 2** in ~120ms.

**Do** write the prompt **inside the launch Shell** (heredoc), then pass
`--prompt-file` (wrapper reads the file; no empty `$(cat)` argv).

1. One Shell command writes + launches (long prompts stay in the heredoc):

```bash
mkdir -p /tmp/sume-opus-prompts
cat > /tmp/sume-opus-prompts/<job-slug>.md <<'EOF'
# Opus: …
Work in **English**. …
EOF
test -s /tmp/sume-opus-prompts/<job-slug>.md
```

`<job-slug>` = 2–4 kebab tokens describing the job (aim for 3), e.g.
`format-uifix-pdp` — **not** issue-only (`2000`). Optional issue suffix:
`format-uifix-pdp-2000`. SoT: orchestration skill § "Worker slug naming".

2. Start with Shell **`block_until_ms: 0`** (background immediately).

   **Terminal title = Shell `description` (required).** Cursor shows this in
   the “N Terminals Running” list — not `--name` alone. Always set
   `description` to the **same string** the Active workers board Job column
   uses:

   ```text
   Opus : <job-slug> (#<issue>)
   ```

   Examples: `Opus : dashboard-ui-chrome (#2819)`,
   `Opus : sentry-cutover-stack (#2828)`.
   No issue yet: `Opus : <job-slug>` (add `(#N)` as soon as the issue exists).
   **Resume / steer:** reuse the **exact same** title — never prose like
   “Relaunch dead…”, “Comment Filter flyout…”, or a bare `# Reopen…` command
   comment (those become unreadable `Cursor (#…)` rows).

```bash
# Shell tool: description = "Opus : <job-slug> (#<issue>)"
# Same command as the heredoc above — one Shell, then:
cd /Users/huhchaewon/sume/sume-com && sume-bg-launch \
  --backend claude --name <job-slug> \
  --prompt-file /tmp/sume-opus-prompts/<job-slug>.md
```

Resume / steer (same session — prefer this over a new worker).
`sume-bg-launch --resume` **kills older wrappers** on that uuid first
(two `grok -p --resume` on one session = empty live log / hang).

```bash
# Shell tool: description = same "Opus : <job-slug> (#<issue>)" as the live job
cd /Users/huhchaewon/sume/sume-com && sume-bg-launch \
  --backend claude --name <job-slug> \
  --resume <session_uuid> \
  --prompt-file /tmp/sume-opus-prompts/<follow-up>.md
```

Grok: `--backend grok` and `description`: `Grok : <job-slug> (#N)`,
backend flags after `--` (`-- --effort high`).

Use the **same `cd` repo path** the original session used, or resume fails.

3. **Required smoke (once, not a poll):** read the new terminal file.
   Alive = `📎 session_id=` (or wrapper `—— agent live ——` + grok/claude lines).
   Dead = `exit_code` in ~1s (usually 2 + `missing prompt` / `not found`).
   Dead → fix the prompt file and relaunch **this turn**. Do not tell Chase
   the worker is up. Then **stop waiting**. Do not poll for completion.

4. Tell the user briefly:
   - what started + title (`Opus : <job-slug> (#N)`) / `--name`
   - `session_id=…`
   - live log: wrapper prints `live_log: …/opus-live/<stamp>-<name>.log`
   - watch: `tail -f ~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/state/opus-live/LATEST.log`

5. End your turn or do other work. Completion arrives as a **system
   notification** on the background Shell task — that is the monitor.

## On completion notification

1. Read the finished terminal file (or live log).
2. Use only `📎 session_id=` + the `—— final ——` block (not the whole tool dump).
3. Brief user status in their language.
4. Immediately run any **already-authorized** follow-up (e.g. "끝나면 resume로
   mega-issue → BP → PR"). Do not re-ask.

## Status when the user asks "어때?"

One-shot only — `tail` ~20–40 lines of the live log or terminal file, summarize.
No `sleep` loops, no repeated `AwaitShell` polling.

## Recover a forgotten session_id

```bash
claude-human-stream --sessions
# or: rg 'session_id=' ~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/state/opus-live/
# or: rg '📎 session_id=' <finished-terminal>.txt
```

Prefer `--resume <uuid>` over `--continue` (continue = most recent in **this cwd** only).

## When steering a live Opus session

If you `--resume` with a **STEERING UPDATE** that replaces an in-flight mandate,
**kill the previous background Shell** for that worker (its `pid` from the
terminals file / process tree) so two wrappers do not fight over the same
Claude session. Keep only the steered Shell alive. Do this in the same turn
as the steer launch — do not leave the old terminal running.

## Forbidden (this is why other threads fail)

| Bad | Why | Do instead |
|-----|-----|------------|
| Cursor `Task` + `claude-opus-*` | Wrong transport; burns Cursor Opus | `claude-human-stream` Shell |
| Cursor `Task` + `cursor-grok-*` | Wrong transport; Grok Build is the desk harness | `agent-human-stream --backend grok` |
| Shell with default/long `block_until_ms` | Job is minutes–hours; tool times out / looks "stuck" | `block_until_ms: 0` |
| `AwaitShell` / sleep until done | Turns main into a polling loop; user said not to wait | Completion notification |
| `claude-human-stream --cwd …` | Flag does not exist | `cd … && claude-human-stream` |
| Fresh Opus when user said "resume" | Loses audit/BP context | `--resume <uuid>` same cwd |
| Inline mega-prompt in Shell arg | Quoting/length failures | heredoc in the **same** Shell + `--prompt-file` |
| `Write` prompt + parallel `$(cat)` | File not visible yet → exit 2 `missing prompt` | One Shell: heredoc then `--prompt-file` |
| Second `--resume` without killing the first | Empty live log / hung grok | `sume-bg-launch --resume` (stops old wrappers) |
| Dump full Opus tool log into chat | Noise | `—— final ——` only |
| Claim done before notification | False completion | Wait for `exit_code` / final block |
| `--name 2000` / issue-only labels | Chase can't skim terminal list | `format-uifix-pdp` (+ optional `-2000`) |
| Prose / command Shell `description` | UI shows “Create arch…” / `Cursor (#…)` ≠ board job | `description`: `Opus : <job-slug> (#N)` |

## Parallelism

- Multiple Opus / Grok Build jobs: multiple background Shells, distinct `--name`s.
- Grok land / Grok author: **`agent-human-stream --backend grok`** (same
  Shell recipe). Do **not** use Cursor `Task` / `cursor-grok-*`.
- Composer explore: Cursor `Task` (`explore`) — also background.
- Do not block the user turn on a background worker unless they explicitly
  asked to wait, or the next action is hard-blocked on that result.

## Handoff after Opus enqueues MQ (**default**)

**Chase lock (2026-08-05):** Opus authors through **Graphite MQ enqueue**;
Grok **lands**. Always hand off land babysit unless the user explicitly said
Opus owns land for that task.

1. Opus: **fresh clone only** → fix → local green → Graphite open → CI →
   enqueue → **STOP**.
   - **Always:** `gt create` → **`gt submit`** (required). Treat `gt` like
     `gh` — first-class, not optional.
   - **Forbidden:** `git worktree add` under the shared Cursor checkout for
     any `gt` command (shared `.git` trunk poisons submit — #2383).
   - **Forbidden:** `gh pr create` on `sume-com` (single or stack). If
     `gt submit` fails (“trunk out of date”), new fresh clone →
     cherry-pick/track → `gt submit`. Never fall back to `gh`.
   - **After submit:** SAME session — poll **`gt merge --dry-run`** every
     **15–30s** (default **20s**; **never** default `sleep 60+`) until
     ready — **not** `gh pr checks` loops (**no minute cap**) → on dry-run
     ready **immediately** **`gt merge --no-interactive`** (same clone).
     Fallback: `gh pr edit <N> --add-label merge-queue`.
   - **On dry-run `Required checks failed`:** **break immediately** — do
     **not** keep polling Ready. Act: ≤2 `gh run rerun --failed` for known
     flake, else minimal CI unblock → `gt submit` → dry-run → merge.
     **Forbidden:** sleep/dry-run-only while last dry-run already failed.
   - **Repo CI flake:** shifting timeouts / same fail on unrelated PRs →
     **≤2 reruns**, then **minimal CI unblock commit** allowed (e.g. vitest
     `testTimeout`). **Forbidden:** endless `gh run rerun` with no code
     change. Still blocked → `HANDOFF: grok-ci-merge` (`sume-gt-mq` § F).
   - **PR-A/B/C train:** all layers in one session → `gt submit --stack` →
     dry-run ready → **`gt merge`** for the whole train. Do **not** “open A
     only → merge → resume for B”.
   - **STOP** immediately after enqueue confirmed (QUEUED / label /
     Graphite activity) with **`LANDED: no` + `NOT 완료`**. Do **not**
     babysit MQ draft CI / `main` tip / restack-while-merging unless
     this session owns land. **Do not tell Chase 완료.**
   - Opus prompt **must** include: `Required skill: read
     ~/.agents/skills/sume-gt-mq/SKILL.md before any gt submit/merge` plus
     the GRAPHITE hard-lock block from orchestration § "Delegation checklist"
     / `sume-gt-mq` (incl. **poll ≤30s + dry-run → merge**, **no exit
     before enqueue evidence**).
   - Follow BP / issue locks exactly.
   - Done report: clone path + Graphite URL + GitHub PR URL + enqueue
     evidence + **`LANDED: no` + `NOT 완료`** + `HANDOFF: grok-land`.
2. Main agent: on Opus completion (enqueue done), launch **Grok Build** via
   `agent-human-stream --backend grok` (**Shell `block_until_ms: 0`**,
   title `Grok : <job-slug> (#N)`) to babysit land → deploy.
   **Do not tell Chase 완료** until `origin/main` has `(#N)`.
   - **Default:** MQ already enqueued — watch draft CI → **stay until**
     `main` tip `(#N)` (re-enqueue on eject; do not STOP at enqueue) →
     issue comment / authorized ops. Do **not** re-enqueue if still in MQ.
   - **Fallback** (`HANDOFF: grok-ci-merge`): Opus could not enqueue → CI
     green → `gh pr edit <N> --add-label merge-queue` (no clone) → land.
   - If Opus only opened via `gh pr create`: **reject** — repair with
     fresh-clone `gt submit` before enqueue.
   - After restack: **`gt submit` again**, then Opus (or fallback Grok)
     re-enqueues.
   - Landed / Chase **완료** = commit on `origin/main` with `(#N)`;
     Graphite FF may show GitHub `CLOSED` / `mergedAt: null`. Enqueue,
     green PR checks, and Graphite “Your changes” are **not** 완료.
   - Never mid-stack GitHub-only squash; never sibling `main` PRs on one train.
3. Do **not** leave Opus long-polling land after enqueue. If an Opus session
   is already on land babysit, **kill that Shell** and reassign to Grok
   (same turn). Grok land must **not** exit at enqueue. Surface the MQ
   draft URL; intervene on red / eject; stay until `origin/main` `(#N)`.

